{
  "composition_summary": "Reviewed the single user request and drafted exactly one class-22 pure-logic component pc-check-retry-eligibility. The body is module-scope Python with a direct result assignment on every path: it reads all required fields via inputs.get (so missing/null/invalid fail closed without raising), validates types and bounds before any comparison, and returns retry only when outcome is retryable, attempt < max_attempts, state is not completed, and (read_only or dedup_verified) is true. Completed effects never replay. No imports, I/O, host calls, or LLM use. The description retains the live global Tool policy, cancellation, resource limits, attempt-freshness and deduplication-evidence checks, and notes the typed-runner/inputs interface is a target contract requiring runtime support. The host sink supports class 22 with name/description/content, so the payload is emitted; proposed_recipe_updates, proposed_intent_examples, settings_adjustments and adjusted_volatile_messages remain empty, and no conversation history was altered.",
  "proposed_components": [
    {
      "class_code": 22,
      "payload": {
        "name": "pc-check-retry-eligibility",
        "description": "Deterministic pure-logic guard that decides whether a logical step invocation is eligible for a bounded retry, before any dispatch is attempted. It returns retry only when the outcome is retryable, the attempt count is below max_attempts, the operation state is not completed, and read_only or dedup_verified is true. Completed effects never replay even when read_only/dedup_verified are true. This is evidence-conditioned pure logic, not dispatch permission: it does not grant dispatch, replace live policy, cancellation, resource limits, attempt freshness or actual deduplication evidence. The consuming Recipe/runner must still check current instance-wide Tool policy, cancellation and fresh execution identity before every permitted retry, and reconcile unknown completion through a supported path rather than inferring no-effect from a missing completion record. The typed inputs interface (operation_state, outcome, attempt, max_attempts, read_only, dedup_verified) is a target contract requiring actual runner support; booleans are exact booleans, not truthy strings/numbers/lists, and missing/null/invalid data fails closed. No I/O, imports or host calls.",
        "content": "operation_state = inputs.get('operation_state')\noutcome = inputs.get('outcome')\nattempt = inputs.get('attempt')\nmax_attempts = inputs.get('max_attempts')\nread_only = inputs.get('read_only')\ndedup_verified = inputs.get('dedup_verified')\nvalid = (\n    type(operation_state) is str and operation_state in ('completed', 'unknown', 'not_started')\n    and type(outcome) is str and outcome in ('retryable', 'terminal')\n    and type(attempt) is int and not isinstance(attempt, bool) and attempt >= 1\n    and type(max_attempts) is int and not isinstance(max_attempts, bool) and max_attempts >= 1\n    and type(read_only) is bool\n    and type(dedup_verified) is bool\n)\nretry = False\nif valid:\n    retry = (outcome == 'retryable' and attempt < max_attempts and operation_state != 'completed' and (read_only or dedup_verified))\nresult = {'retry': retry}"
      }
    }
  ],
  "settings_adjustments": [],
  "proposed_recipe_updates": [],
  "bridge_messages": [],
  "adjusted_volatile_messages": [
    ["user", "We need a reusable deterministic guard before considering a retry."]
  ]
,
  "proposed_intent_examples": []
}
